er`,map:`farm`,drone:0,mode:`acro`,summary:`Acro mode is how FPV pilots really fly. The quad stays where you put it.`,intro:[`In acro (rate) mode the sticks set how fast the quad rotates, not what angle it sits at. Let go and it holds whatever angle it is at, even upside down.`,`This is what every freestyle and racing pilot uses. It feels wild at first, then it becomes the only way you want to fly.`],tips:[`Tilt forward a little, then centre the stick: the quad keeps that tilt and flies forward.`,`Throttle now controls height AND speed together. Fly a steady forward tilt and use throttle to stay level.`,`Your camera is tilted up (uptilt). Fast flight looks level on screen when the quad is pitched well forward.`],objectives:[{type:`gates`,text:`Fly the line of hoops`,gates:[Xv(0,-25,2,3.5),Xv(0,-55,3,3.5),Xv(4,-85,3,3.5),Xv(14,-115,2.5,3.5),Xv(30,-140,2.5,3.5)]}],medals:[16,24,40]},{id:`l4-turns`,title:`Coordinated turns`,level:`Intermediate`,map:`farm`,drone:0,mode:`acro`,summary:`Turn like a pro: roll into the turn, pull with pitch, guide with yaw.`,intro:[`Beginners turn with yaw alone and the quad skids sideways. Real pilots roll into the turn, then pull back on pitch to carve around it, with a touch of yaw in the same direction.`,`It is the same as a plane banking. The tighter the turn, the more you roll and pull.`],tips:[`Roll first, then pull. Yaw just keeps the nose tidy.`,`Add throttle in the turn: a banked quad loses lift.`,`Look at the exit of the turn, not the hoop you are in.`],objectives:[{type:`gates`,text:`Slalom through the hoops`,gates:[Xv(-8,-25,2),Xv(8,-45,2),Xv(-8,-65,2),Xv(8,-85,2),Xv(-8,-105,2),Xv(0,-125,2)]}],medals:[14,20,32]},{id:`l5-throttle`,title:`Throttle control`,level:`Intermediate`,map:`farm`,drone:0,mode:`acro`,summary:`High, low, high, low. Manage height with throttle while flying fast.`,intro:[`Smooth throttle is what separates good pilots from great ones. Every change in tilt needs a change in throttle.`,`These hoops alternate between skimming the grass and 7 metres up.`],tips:[`To drop: ease off the throttle, then catch it early, before you reach the hoop.`,`To climb: punch the throttle before you need the height, not during.`,`Watch the ALT on the OSD while you learn.`],objectives:[{type:`gates`,text:`Low, high, low, high…`,gates:[Xv(0,-25,.4),Xv(0,-50,7),Xv(0,-75,.4),Xv(0,-100,7),Xv(0,-125,.4),Xv(0,-150,4)]}],medals:[12,18,30]},{id:`l6-flips`,title:`Flips and rolls`,level:`Intermediate`,map:`farm`,drone:0,mode:`acro`,summary:`Your first tricks. Climb, flip, catch it.`,intro:[`A flip is a full 360° turn on the pitch axis; a roll is the same on the roll axis. The secret is the throttle: punch up, cut throttle while you rotate, then punch again to catch the fall.`,`Climb high first. You have more time than you think.`],tips:[`Punch up to 15-20 m, then throttle to almost zero before you flip.`,`Full stick for the rotation, centre it as the horizon comes back.`,`Catch with throttle the moment you are upright.`],objectives:[{type:`rotate`,text:`Do a full flip (pitch 360°)`,axis:`pitch`,turns:1,withinSec:2.5},{type:`rotate`,text:`Do a full roll (roll 360°)`,axis:`roll`,turns:1,withinSec:2.5}],medals:[20,35,60]},{id:`l7-powerloop`,title:`Power loop`,level:`Advanced`,map:`farm`,drone:0,mode:`acro`,summary:`Through the gate, up and over the top, and through it again.`,intro:[`The power loop is the classic freestyle move: fly through a gap, pull up into a full loop over the top of it and come back through the same gap.`,`Throttle up as you pull, ease off at the top, let gravity bring you round, then catch it on the way down.`],tips:[`Enter with speed. A slow loop is a short loop.`,`Pull back on pitch smoothly; the camera uptilt makes the top of the loop look early.`,`Look for the gate as you come over the top.`],objectives:[{type:`loop`,text:`Power loop the hoop: through, up and over, and through again`,gate:{kind:`hoop`,x:0,z:-30,elev:1.5,size:3.5,yaw:0,color:`purple`},minClimb:5}],medals:[10,18,35